  "description": "<p>When attempting to rebuild the fedora db, I am getting the following error on my very first object:</p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-none\">ERROR 18:53:10.880 [ReindexWorker-2] (ReindexWorker) Reindexing of OCFL id info:fedora/17/db/8e/98/17db8e98-3746-4cc1-9a65-5e967c2c47a4 failed\nfcrepo_1      | org.fcrepo.storage.ocfl.exception.ValidationException: OCFL object info:fedora/17/db/8e/98/17db8e98-3746-4cc1-9a65-5e967c2c47a4 is not a valid Fedora 6 object. The following problems were identified:\nfcrepo_1      |   1. [Version v1] Missing root header file at .fcrepo/fcr-root.json\nfcrepo_1      | \tat org.fcrepo.storage.ocfl.exception.ValidationException.createForObject(ValidationException.java:60)\nfcrepo_1      | \tat org.fcrepo.storage.ocfl.validation.Context.throwValidationException(Context.java:76)\nfcrepo_1      | \tat org.fcrepo.storage.ocfl.validation.ObjectValidator$ObjectValidatorInner.validate(ObjectValidator.java:118)\nfcrepo_1      | \tat org.fcrepo.storage.ocfl.validation.ObjectValidator.validate(ObjectValidator.java:85)\nfcrepo_1      | \tat org.fcrepo.persistence.ocfl.impl.ReindexService.indexOcflObject(ReindexService.java:109)\nfcrepo_1      | \tat org.fcrepo.persistence.ocfl.impl.ReindexWorker.lambda$run$0(ReindexWorker.java:118)\nfcrepo_1      | \tat org.fcrepo.common.db.DbTransactionExecutor.lambda$doInTx$3(DbTransactionExecutor.java:91)\nfcrepo_1      | \tat org.springframework.transaction.support.TransactionOperations.lambda$executeWithoutResult$0(TransactionOperations.java:68)\nfcrepo_1      | \tat org.springframework.transaction.support.TransactionTemplate.execute(TransactionTemplate.java:140)\nfcrepo_1      | \tat org.springframework.transaction.support.TransactionOperations.executeWithoutResult(TransactionOperations.java:67)\nfcrepo_1      | \tat org.fcrepo.common.db.DbTransactionExecutor.doInTx(DbTransactionExecutor.java:90)\nfcrepo_1      | \tat org.fcrepo.common.db.DbTransactionExecutor.lambda$doInTxWithRetry$2(DbTransactionExecutor.java:74)\nfcrepo_1      | \tat net.jodah.failsafe.Functions.lambda$toSupplier$10(Functions.java:240)\nfcrepo_1      | \tat net.jodah.failsafe.Functions.lambda$get$0(Functions.java:48)\nfcrepo_1      | \tat net.jodah.failsafe.RetryPolicyExecutor.lambda$supply$0(RetryPolicyExecutor.java:62)\nfcrepo_1      | \tat net.jodah.failsafe.Execution.executeSync(Execution.java:129)\nfcrepo_1      | \tat net.jodah.failsafe.FailsafeExecutor.call(FailsafeExecutor.java:376)\nfcrepo_1      | \tat net.jodah.failsafe.FailsafeExecutor.run(FailsafeExecutor.java:210)\nfcrepo_1      | \tat org.fcrepo.common.db.DbTransactionExecutor.doInTxWithRetry(DbTransactionExecutor.java:73)\nfcrepo_1      | \tat org.fcrepo.persistence.ocfl.impl.ReindexWorker.run(ReindexWorker.java:117)\nfcrepo_1      | \tat java.base/java.lang.Thread.run(Thread.java:834)\nfcrepo_1      | ERROR 18:53:10.882 [ReindexWorker-0] (ReindexWorker) Reindexing of OCFL id info:fedora/2022-03/50761-Service File.jpg failed</pre>\n</div></div>\n\n\n\n<p>After talking to <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=5b44cac50a894e589871012b\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"5b44cac50a894e589871012b\" data-account-id=\"5b44cac50a894e589871012b\" accountid=\"5b44cac50a894e589871012b\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Peter Winckles</a> in Slack, I <tt>tree</tt>'d the approriate directory and got</p>\n\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-none\">root@islandora01:/mnt/fedora-datastreamStore/fcrepo-data/home/data/ocfl-root/8ec/dd3/663/8ecdd3663573ebe4e39e550741f17f1ce781fc33b9fe078cb61400116d928240# tree -a .\n.\n├── 0=ocfl_object_1.0\n├── extensions\n│   └── 0005-mutable-head\n│       ├── head\n│       │   ├── content\n│       │   │   └── r1\n│       │   │       ├── fcr-container.nt\n│       │   │       └── .fcrepo\n│       │   │           └── fcr-root.json\n│       │   ├── inventory.json\n│       │   └── inventory.json.sha512\n│       ├── revisions\n│       │   └── r1\n│       └── root-inventory.json.sha512\n├── inventory.json\n├── inventory.json.sha512\n└── v1\n    ├── inventory.json\n    └── inventory.json.sha512\n\n8 directories, 11 files</pre>\n</div></div>\n\n<p>According to him, it appears to be a bug in the validation code.  It is not accounting for an empty v1 when manual versioning is used.</p>",
